# Angular RSS 2025 - Development Context & Rules

## Project Overview

This is an Angular 20.1.0 RSS reader application built with TypeScript, following modern Angular patterns and best practices.

## Angular Development Best Practices

### TypeScript Configuration

- Always use `strict: true` type checking
- Prefer type inference when obvious
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` with type guards instead
- Use proper interfaces and types for RSS data structures

### Component Architecture

- **Always use standalone components** (Angular 15+ pattern)
- Use **signals** and `computed()` for reactive state management
- Implement `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` for performance
- Keep components small and single-responsibility
- Use `input()` and `output()` functions instead of decorators
- Prefer inline templates for small components

### Modern Template Syntax

- Use **native control flow**: `@if`, `@for`, `@switch` instead of `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`
- Use `[class]` and `[style]` bindings instead of `ngClass` and `ngStyle`
- Use `async` pipe for observables
- Avoid complex logic in templates

### Service Patterns

- Design services with single responsibility
- Use `providedIn: 'root'` for singleton services
- Use `inject()` function instead of constructor injection
- Implement proper error handling for RSS feeds

### State Management

- Use **signals** for local component state
- Use `computed()` for derived values
- Keep state pure and predictable
- Use RxJS only when necessary (HTTP calls, complex async operations)

### Performance & Assets

- Use `NgOptimizedImage` for all static images
- Implement lazy loading for feature routes
- Use OnPush change detection strategy
- Implement virtual scrolling for large RSS feed lists

## RSS-Specific Patterns

### Data Models

```typescript
interface RSSFeed {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  url: string;
  description?: string;
  lastUpdated: Date;
  isActive: boolean;
}

interface RSSItem {
  id: string;
  feedId: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  link: string;
  publishDate: Date;
  isRead: boolean;
}
```

### Service Architecture

- **FeedService**: Centralized RSS feed management
- **RSSParserService**: XML parsing and format handling
- **StorageService**: Local storage and caching
- **ErrorHandlerService**: Global error handling

### Component Structure

```
App Component (Root)
├── Header Component
├── Sidebar Component (Feed Navigation)
├── Main Content Area
│   ├── Feed List Component
│   ├── Article List Component
│   └── Article Detail Component
└── Footer Component
```

